<p>Hey <%= @user.first_name_or_fallback %>,</p>

<p>
  <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "This app is" : "These apps are" %> still connected to your Dabble Me account
  (<%= @user.email %>) and can read and add to your journal, but
  <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "hasn't" : "haven't" %> been used in over a year:
</p>

<ul>
  <% @stale_apps.each do |stale_app| %>
    <% hosts = Admin::OauthApps.redirect_hosts(stale_app.application) %>
    <li>
      <strong><%= stale_app.application.name.truncate(60) %></strong><%= " (#{hosts.first(2).join(', ')})" if hosts.any? %>:
      last used <%= stale_app.last_used_at.strftime("%B %Y") %>, added <%= stale_app.application.created_at.strftime("%B %Y") %>
    </li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<p>
  If you don't use <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "it" : "them" %> anymore, remove
  <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "it" : "them" %> from
  <%= link_to "Connected apps", security_url(anchor: "connected-apps") %>.
  A removed app loses access right away, and you can connect it again any time.
</p>

<p>
  Still using <%= @stale_apps.one? ? "it" : "them" %>? You don't need to do anything.
</p>

<p>
  <br>
  Thanks,
  <br>
  Dabble Me
</p>
